{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "13", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "05", "M": "28", "S": "37"}}, "news": [{"title": "About 180 properties in Gurugram served notices for flouting building code", "para": "Authorities in Gurugram are stepping up their efforts against illegal building practices and property misuse by issuing notices to violators. Following the Supreme Court's mandate, survey teams are meticulously inspecting licensed colonies. Those found in violation of regulations are at risk of facing serious actions, including possible sealing or demolition of illegal constructions. The initiative aims to guarantee compliance with established building plans and appropriate property usage.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/about-180-properties-in-gurugram-served-notices-for-flouting-building-code/133197765?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-251196/133197765.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Pilani Investment to sell 1.7 million UltraTech Cement shares for \u20b91,908 crore", "para": "Pilani Investment plans to sell 1.7 million UltraTech Cement shares valued at \u20b91,908 crore on August 13, 2026, at a 3% discount. Separately, UltraTech Cement is acquiring a 26% stake in Solaris Horizon Energy to support its green energy initiatives.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/cement/pilani-investment-to-sell-1-7-million-ultratech-cement-shares-for-1908-crore/133197183?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-72266/133197183.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "cement"}, {"title": "Two-storey dwelling units can now be redeveloped: Delhi development body", "para": "The Delhi Development Authority has sanctioned a policy focused on the overhaul of outdated two-storey residential units, with plans for broader application across the city. This will streamline building plan approvals by eliminating NOC requirements across multiple departments. Additionally, a crucial land use alteration for a metro depot in Narela Sub-City was approved, which aims to boost connectivity and promote regional growth.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/two-storey-dwelling-units-can-now-be-redeveloped-delhi-development-body/133197149?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-312300/133197149.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}